<h2>Catechist's Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">For class preparation and delivery. For the catechist's use only.</p>

<h3>Class Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated duration:</strong> 60 minutes</p>
<p><strong>Central theme:</strong> The human person, created in the image of God, possesses an inviolable dignity that grounds all Christian morality.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>Understand that human dignity comes from being created in the image of God (Gn 1:26-27).</li>
  <li>Recognize that original sin wounded dignity but did not destroy it.</li>
  <li>Discover that Christ's redemption restores and elevates our dignity.</li>
  <li>Learn to live according to one's own dignity and respect that of others.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key verse:</strong> &laquo;God created man in his own image; in the image of God he created him; male and female he created them&raquo; (Gn 1:27)</p>
<p><strong>CCC references:</strong> 1700-1715</p>
</section>

